  "notes": [
    "Van Eeghenstraat 97-101 (pand 0363100012237151, built 1900): a pair of eclectic villa-houses and a narrow third house facing the Vondelpark across Van Eeghenstraat.",
    "walls[0] the pair's front (panel 8, 14.5 m; crop w01-335p 2022-03-22, sunlit, a parked van over the ground storey): red-brown brick with thin cream speklagen, a grey stone ground storey, segmental heads with cream voussoirs, five window columns; a canted white bay window on the first floor at the left with a wrought-iron balcony on its roof, a square white oriel on the first floor at the right with a white balustrade on its roof (oriel lists and oriel roof rails added to the kit for this front); stepped and towered gables over the cornice.",
    "walls[1] number 101 (panel 6, 6.7 m; crop w03-338w 2022-03-22): yellow-buff brick with red bands, a white oriel on the second floor with a balustrade, stone ground storey.",
    "INFERRED: the rear and party walls (otherWalls brick grid)."
